---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { legalCompany, legalMailto } from "../lib/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy choices — Zenguy"
  description="Controls for account deletion, optional AI processing, notifications and privacy rights in Zenguy."
  heading="Privacy choices"
  effective="2 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    These controls apply to the Zenguy service and iOS companion app. They are
    described in detail in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete your account</h2>
  <p>
    Open <strong>More → Account → Delete my account</strong> in the signed-in
    iOS app. Confirm with the current password and the word DELETE. Sessions and
    push tokens are revoked, memberships are removed, and owned workspaces are
    made inaccessible and purged. The policy explains the limited legal and
    security records that may be retained in anonymized form. The app does not
    require you to contact support to complete deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose whether OpenAI may process test data</h2>
  <p>
    OpenAI processing starts off. Zenguy runs browser tests on an isolated
    runner in Cloudflare Containers that uses the OpenAI API, so without a
    current consent no browser test runs in the workspace. A workspace Owner or
    Admin can review the exact categories and purpose in
    <strong>More → AI data sharing</strong> in the iOS app or
    <strong>Workspace Settings → AI data sharing</strong> in the web
    application, give an affirmative consent, or revoke it later. Without a
    current consent, the backend does not release the run to the runner or to OpenAI.
    Configured secret values are never released to OpenAI.
  </p>

  <h2>Push notifications and biometrics</h2>
  <p>
    Push is optional and can be disabled for the device in Account or in iOS
    Settings. Removing the device or deleting the account deletes its Zenguy
    push-token record. App Lock can be disabled in Account. Face ID and Touch ID
    matching happen on the device; Zenguy does not receive biometric templates.
  </p>

  <h2>Access, correction, export and objection</h2>
  <p>
    To exercise GDPR access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability
    or objection rights, or to withdraw another consent, email
    <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>. We may ask for information
    needed to verify identity. You can also complain to the Spanish Data
    Protection Agency (AEPD) or another competent EU supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics choices</h2>
  <p>
    The iOS app contains no Google Analytics SDK. The website and web
    application keep optional Google Analytics off until consent is given on
    that origin. Use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the website footer or
    <strong>Cookie preferences</strong> in the web application to change that
    choice. Required first-party security and service-activity records are
    explained in the Privacy Policy and are not used for advertising.
  </p>
</Legal>
